==============================================================================
M-005  is_invalidated(hit, hit's OWN confirming close)
==============================================================================
  Flag +1        index=9 dir=+1 invalidation=112.0/DOWN confirming close=109.5
     is_invalidated(hit, its OWN confirming close) -> True
  -> select_native_pattern() rejects a hit when ANY bar from hit.index
     onward invalidates it, so a self-invalidating hit is unreachable.

==============================================================================
M-006  _triangle scans j from 1, so a breakout can predate the pattern
==============================================================================
  swing highs [(4, 110.0), (8, 110.0), (12, 110.0)]
  swing lows  [(2, 99.0), (5, 90.0), (9, 92.0), (13, 94.0)]
  detect_triangle_ascending -> None
  the loop bound in _triangle: ['for j in range(max(flat_vals and 1, 1), len(closes)):', 'for j in range(len(closes) - 1, -1, -1):']
  `max(flat_vals and 1, 1)` evaluates to max(1,1)=1 whenever flat_vals
  is a non-empty list, so the scan starts at bar 1, not after formation.
  19-bar window hit index=None | 25-bar window hit index=None
